{
 "id": "rewrite/replay-at-new-position/hot/5m",
 "description": "The same 6,000-token output appears at message 3 and at message 8. extract_llm compacted message 3 when it arrived, so the provider holds the compacted form there and the replay is free of any break. Message 8 was not compacted on arrival (the operator was throttled). On request 2 the operator compacts it inside the cached prefix: a second change with its own ChangeID saves 5,500 x $0.30 = +$0.00165 and breaks the 4,500 tokens from message 8 to the end of the prefix, 4,500 x $3.45 = -$0.01553: the break is larger than the saving, which is the cost issue 199 hid. The replay of the first change stays break-free.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#199",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "beforeBStar",
  "cache": "hit-hit-break",
  "ttl": "5m",
  "lifetime": "exact",
  "break": "plugin",
  "replay": "true"
 },
 "rates": "fixture-v1",
 "open": [
  "design \u00a75.1 snaps B* to the last client breakpoint at or before the previous body's end, and the client's breakpoints are the current request's own: system and the new last message. Read literally that gives the end of system, not the end of the previous body. The examples, and this case, take the end of the previous body."
 ],
